Instead of a typical post to social media, the South African artist got creative to showcase the tracklist. She headed to a blacklight room and spray-painted each song title on the walls in fluorescent colors while her &#8220;She Did It Again&#8221; collaboration with Zara Larsson provided the soundtrack.

The album is 14 tracks and boasts previously released singles including &#8220;Chanel,&#8221; &#8220;Is It,&#8221; &#8220;Is It Love&#8221; and &#8220;She Did It Again.&#8221; Other songs fans can expect include &#8220;That Girl,&#8221; &#8220;Kiss,&#8221; &#8220;Fairytale,&#8221; &#8220;Mr. Nonchalant&#8221; and &#8220;Hot Tubs.&#8221;

&#8220;Chanel&#8221; arrived in October as the project&#8217;s lead single and reached No. 43 on the Billboard Hot 100. It eventually topped the Rhythmic Airplay chart in March, while &#8220;She Did It Again&#8221; peaked at No. 59 on the Hot 100.

Tyla spoke to Billboard Africa earlier in July about the meaning behind A*Pop , as she looks to mesh the worlds of African music and pop.

&#8220; A*Pop is just something that came to me. It just makes so much sense. I&#8217;ve always wanted to be this pop star. I just hate being restricted and limited. I hate following rules. I hate being polished. For a long time, I felt like I had to be something in order to be a pop star,&#8221; she said. &#8220;I bring the A to pop. It&#8217;s African pop; African music is pop music.&#8221;

A*Pop serves as the follow-up to her 2024 self-titled debut, which debuted at No. 24 on the Billboard 200. Tyla also dove into the movie world this year. In June, she made her voice-acting debut in Toy Story 5 as the inflatable flamingo.

